<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Four Year Plan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1936</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Four Year Plan was an economic programme launched by Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in 1936 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hermann-goring">Hermann Göring</a> to make the country ready for war within four years. It sought self-sufficiency in raw materials, building plants for synthetic fuel and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> and exploiting low-grade iron ore, and it gave Göring wide control over the economy at the expense of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hjalmar-schacht">Hjalmar Schacht</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/four-year-plan.jpg" alt="Four Year Plan" width="320" height="302" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rijksmuseum · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Document_met_bericht_aan_M.J._Sanou,_NG-1980-5-B-3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
